Unbound Upstream via Gateway Plugin

Forwards Unbound's root zone to a resolver that is reached through a
gateway group, using the group's best member, and switches to another
member when the best one changes. The resolver is reached by a host route
and a firewall rule the plugin adds for it, so its queries leave through
that member's tunnel and never the WAN.

- When no member is usable or the resolver stops answering, the root zone
  returns to Unbound's own forwarders (or to recursion), without flushing
  the cache; a recovered member is used again only after a failback delay
- Plan and log only (dry run) is the default; nothing changes in Unbound
  or the routing table until it is turned off
- Never writes the configuration at run time: the only writer is Save
- Can POST each switch to a URL, and has a read-only status privilege
  for pollers such as Home Assistant

Plugin Changelog
================

1.3

Security release.

* The block follows the address the plugin last used, not only the
  setting: disabling the plugin, changing the resolver address or
  removing the package keeps that address blocked (and the route's
  device passed) until a stop has really undone it. The minute job
  stays installed while such an address remains, and the filter is
  reloaded when that address changes
* A stop that cannot restore Unbound's forwarders through its control
  channel ends in Unbound's own start, which applies the root zone you
  configured (every requested stop and the package removal; a requested
  stop does so unless the cache is flushed on a restart). When even that
  leaves Unbound on the resolver, the removal installs a reject route
  and logs what to run. The removal waits up to 120 s for the lock and
  asks core to reload the filter and restart cron, with core's own
  scripts when configd does not answer. An upgrade still removes the old
  package first, so it falls back to Unbound's own forwarders for 30 to
  60 s
* The page decodes status text with one plain function and no HTML
  parser
* Answers from Unbound's forward list and the configured root zone's
  forward-addr values are admitted by shape only (address, optional
  port, optional host name); an unknown zone option is reported as
  "unknown option", never by its text
* Settings read from a restored configuration (resolver, probe name,
  failback delay, gateway group, notify URL) are checked again where
  they are used; curl speaks only http and https, with no redirects
* A failed notification names only the receiver's scheme, host and port
  (it used to log the whole URL)
* State, record and zone files are read as regular files only, never
  through a link, at most 1 MiB each; pfctl's error file lives in the
  plugin's root-only run directory
* Control characters are replaced in log lines (a line break by "; ", any other by "?")
* Every copyright header reads "Copyright (C) 2026 cayossarian"

1.2_1

* A rules listing cut short by a filter reload, even one that leaves
  the ruleset unchanged, is listed again instead of being judged
* A missing-rules verdict is checked again at every evaluation, instead
  of holding the fallback until the next ruleset change

1.2

* The firewall rules are verified once per ruleset change, keyed by
  pf's ruleset checksum, instead of listing every rule twice on each
  status: the status answers in well under a second (it took about
  5 s)
* A counting block on a table the plugin fills (__unboundupstream_block,
  holding the resolver address) sits ahead of 1.1's block, which stays
  as the backstop. The page's blocked count is that table's counter;
  if the table is flushed the backstop still drops, the page reads
  "counter not armed", and the next evaluation refills it
* The page shows "Healthy for" and "Last down"
* Notify URL: an ordinary setting the page shows after saving, and a
  failed POST's warning names the whole URL
* A contract failure reads "Tunnel mode refused: ..." on the page, as
  not every failure is a change in core

1.1

* Status privilege "Status: Unbound DNS: Upstream via Gateway (API)":
  reads the status and nothing else, for a poller's API key
* Notify on switch: POST each switch between a member and the fallback
  to a URL as JSON
* The status names the resolver address
* Fix: the gateway monitor hook threw a TypeError (a PHP crash report)
  when core reloaded routing in full, which passes no gateway names,
  and dropped that evaluation; it now takes every form core passes

1.0_3

* Menu: the log sits after Unbound's own Log File, and the settings page
  right after Query Forwarding

1.0_2

* A stop logs its cause: a stop from the service or configctl, a package
  removal or a changed resolver address no longer logs "disabled in
  settings" while the plugin is enabled

1.0_1

* Log lines carry the program name dnsupstream: as unboundupstream they
  also landed in Unbound's own log, whose filter selects every program
  name containing "unbound". The log page and its files are unchanged

1.0

* Initial release
